Z||000002||theogre||05-22-2001||09:27 AM||||It will not be plug and play under any conditions. nearly the whole car is wired diferant in 87-88 4 cyl's.<P>With the ease that the DIS motor can be found in other GM product.... This isn't worth the trouble. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-22-2001||09:42 AM||||Thanks, Ogre. I was afraid that might be the case.<BR>I was considering a swap to the older style block because I was intrigued by the idea of installing the Chevy marine crank, and internals, as some others are doing. Could make for one hell of a sleeper. <BR>As you reminded me earlier, I can't do that with DIS.<BR>Back to the drawing board...<BR>    <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
